{"type":"message","id":"43919f21","parentId":"6132a99f","timestamp":"2026-04-02T00:04:43.088Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_WXV31KTwgFGUjzto0eSpof1n|fc_063f6e7d06c593d70169cdb298b0dc819188c0c73bc670cf78","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/ \\\"openclaw/openclaw\\\" Feishu bug 2026.4.1\",\n  \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n  \"count\": 0,\n  \"tookMs\": 1454,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": []\n}"}],"details":{"query":"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/ \"openclaw/openclaw\" Feishu bug 2026.4.1","provider":"tavily","count":0,"tookMs":1454,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"tavily","wrapped":true},"results":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775088282493}}
{"type":"message","id":"89922280","parentId":"43919f21","timestamp":"2026-04-02T00:04:43.773Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_w8nh0WRqyjCzDalQTTM0HMU9|fc_063f6e7d06c593d70169cdb298b0e481919efc18cbc187da57","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/ weixin openclaw 2026.4.1\",\n  \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 2689,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c7ce2226dfe33b97\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 · Issue #52341 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c7ce2226dfe33b97\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52341\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3375503afe158b2a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# [Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 #52341. [[Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14](#top)#52341. After installing `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin@1.0.2` into a local OpenClaw `2026.3.14` source checkout on macOS 26.2, the Weixin plugin does not load consistently: gateway startup logs `Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'` or `Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk/core'`, and CLI plugin loading logs `TypeError: (0 , _pluginSdk.resolvePreferredOpenClawTmpDir) is not a function`. 5. Observe plugin load failures instead of a stable running Weixin channel. After installation and QR login, the external Weixin plugin should load under both gateway startup and CLI/plugin-registry loading, and `channels status` should show a running Weixin account without plugin load errors. * `Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'`. Related existing issue: #52153 is about proactive sending on Weixin; this report is about plugin loading / SDK compatibility before normal runtime behavior. Affected: local/source OpenClaw installs using the external `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` plugin. Consequence: The Weixin plugin does not load reliably, so the channel cannot be used normally.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3375503afe158b2a\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99989843\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2bdeea3de7927631\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Error running `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp` · Issue #24993 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2bdeea3de7927631\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24993\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8fb44ea9463c8a86\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Bug]: Error running `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp` · Issue #24993 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Error running `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp` #24993. [[Bug]: Error running `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp`](#top)#24993. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. ## Description. opened on Feb 24, 2026. ### Summary. Running `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp` failed with console error, plugin is not installed. ### Steps to reproduce. openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp. * openclaw: 2026.2.22-2. ### Expected behavior. Expect the plugin to be installed. ### Actual behavior. I see below errors in console:. Downloading @openclaw/whatsapp… npm pack failed: npm notice Access token expired or revoked. Please try logging in again. npm notice Access token expired or revoked. Please try logging in again. npm error code E404 npm error 404 Not Found - GET https://registry.npmjs.org/@openclaw%2fwhatsapp - Not found npm error 404 npm error 404 '@openclaw/whatsapp@*' is not in this registry. npm error 404 npm error 404 Note that you can also install from a npm error 404 tarball, folder, http url, or git url. npm error A complete log of this run can be found in: /Users/xxx/.npm/_logs/2026-02-24T03_04_25_974Z-debug-0.log. ### OpenClaw version. ### Operating system. ### Install method. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. ### Additional information. I've previously ran setup via `openclaw onboard --install-daemon`, during channel setup it also got stuck so I skipped it. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8fb44ea9463c8a86\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99983776\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e1aa17649d55afe9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIndependent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat · Issue #52537 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e1aa17649d55afe9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52537\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2647dd2e155be3f7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# Independent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat #52537. Independent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat#52537. Two related issues when using independent agents with the WeChat (openclaw-weixin) channel:. Independent agent does not inherit `agents.defaults.thinkingDefault`. When `thinkingDefault: \\\"off\\\"` is set under `agents.defaults`, independent agents (created via `openclaw agents add`) do **not** inherit this setting. New sessions created by inbound messages from the WeChat channel are missing the `reasoning:off` / `think:off` flag. * Main agent session: `reasoning:off` ✅. * Independent wechat agent session: no flag ❌. openclaw-weixin plugin does not filter thinking/reasoning output. The WeChat plugin (`openclaw-weixin`) transparently forwards the full model response to the WeChat chat, including reasoning/thinking blocks. Grep of the weixin plugin source (`src/`) shows zero references to `thinking` or `reasoning` — no filtering logic exists. 1. Independent agents should inherit `agents.defaults.thinkingDefault` (or support per-agent `thinkingDefault` config). 2. The WeChat plugin should strip thinking/reasoning content from outbound messages, consistent with Telegram behavior.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2647dd2e155be3f7\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9998273\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"979ae33beab3e9ac\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUser-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23) · Issue #53403 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"979ae33beab3e9ac\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53403\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"38ffe6b959dc2d10\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: User-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23) · Issue #53403 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # User-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23) #53403. User-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23)#53403. * OpenClaw 3.23 (ccfeecb) and 3.23-1. * macOS 15.7.4 x64. * Plugin: `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` 1.0.2 / 1.0.3. * Plugin install path: `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/`. 1. Install OpenClaw 3.23. 2. Install any user plugin that imports from `openclaw/plugin-sdk` (e.g. 3. 3. Start or restart the gateway 4. Plugin fails to load: `Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'`. Bundled plugins (feishu, etc.) work fine — the issue only affects user-installed plugins in `~/.openclaw/extensions/`. ## Root Cause. In `pi-embedded-CwMQzdKD.js`, `loadOpenClawPlugins()` calls `buildPluginLoaderAliasMap(modulePath)` where `modulePath` is the plugin file path (e.g. `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/index.ts`). The jiti-based loader uses this to build an alias map for `openclaw/plugin-sdk*` imports. The alias map builder has two resolution paths:. Finds `root-alias.cjs` by walking **up to 6 levels** from the plugin directory. For `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/`:. 1. ~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/ 2. Never reaches `/usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/` → returns `null`. Calls `resolveLoaderPluginSdkPackageRoot()` → `resolveOpenClawPackageRootSync()` starting from plugin dirname, then `findNearestPluginSdkPackageRoot()` (max 12 levels). Same problem — cannot reach the OpenClaw package root from `~/.openclaw/extensions/`. ### Why it worked in 3.13. In 3.13, the alias for `openclaw/plugin-sdk` (main entry only) used a different resolution strategy that could locate the OpenClaw package. In 3.23, both main entry and subpath resolution fail for user-installed plugins. Bundled plugins work because they are located at `/usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions/` — inside the same package tree. 1. **Search the OpenClaw executable's location** as a candidate root in `resolveLoaderPluginSdkPackageRoot()`. 2. **Set `NODE_PATH`** to include the OpenClaw package parent in the gateway LaunchAgent. 3. **Add a config option** like `plugins.sdkPath` pointing to the OpenClaw installation directory. 4. **Extend the directory walk limit** or use `require.resolve()` to find the OpenClaw package from the gateway process itself. cc @X\\\\_Corperation (who reported the same issue in the community). ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"38ffe6b959dc2d10\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9998134\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b616126b34a3ef32\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: local TS extensions importing openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry fail to load on 2026.3.22 · Issue #53002 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b616126b34a3ef32\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53002\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0de54b04a78786f2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# [Bug]: local TS extensions importing openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry fail to load on 2026.3.22 #53002. [[Bug]: local TS extensions importing openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry fail to load on 2026.3.22](#top)#53002. On OpenClaw 2026.3.22, a local extension under `~/.openclaw/extensions//index.ts` that imports `openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry` fails to load because the plugin loader resolves the import to `.../dist/plugin-sdk/root-alias.cjs/plugin-entry` instead of the scoped subpath target. A local extension using the documented SDK import path `openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry` should load successfully, matching the documented plugin authoring flow and prior observed behavior on earlier versions. [plugins] telegram-album-outbound failed to load from /Users/shinya/.openclaw/extensions/telegram-album-outbound/index.ts: Error: Cannot find module '/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/plugin-sdk/root-alias.cjs/plugin-entry' Require stack: - /Users/shinya/.openclaw/extensions/telegram-album-outbound/index.ts. * In the failing case, `openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry` appears to be resolved via the parent alias and incorrectly expanded to `root-alias.cjs/plugin-entry` instead of `dist/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry.js`. [plugins] telegram-album-outbound failed to load from /Users/shinya/.openclaw/extensions/telegram-album-outbound/index.ts: Error: Cannot find module '/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/plugin-sdk/root-alias.cjs/plugin-entry' Require stack: - /Users/shinya/.openclaw/extensions/telegram-album-outbound/index.ts. * [[Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 #52341](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52341) — external plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 with `Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'`. * Always for the observed local extension using `openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry`.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0de54b04a78786f2\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9997818\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fa263311bc584bc3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nv2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13 · Issue #54790 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fa263311bc584bc3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/54790\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d0a34b5f58196055\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: v2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13 · Issue #54790 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. # v2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13 #54790. v2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13#54790. * Install method: `npm install -g openclaw`. * Service management: launchd (`ai.openclaw.gateway`). Upgrading from v2026.3.13 to v2026.3.24 via `openclaw update` caused Gateway crash with multiple packaging/build issues preventing clean restart. ## Issue 1: Gateway crashes during upgrade, launchd fails to auto-restart. **Symptom:** After upgrade, Gateway process terminates. **Root cause:** `npm install -g` overwrites `dist/` in-place while the Gateway is running. [ws] ⇄ res ✗ channels.status 2149ms errorCode=UNAVAILABLE errorMessage=Error: Cannot find module '.../dist/audit-membership-runtime-BT91Am6G.js' imported from '.../dist/reply-Bm8VrLQh.js'. **Workaround:** `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/ai.openclaw.gateway`. **Suggestion:** `openclaw update` should gracefully stop the Gateway before replacing dist files, then restart. ## Issue 2: memory-lancedb plugin fails — `dist/package.json` missing from npm package. [plugins] memory-lancedb failed to load: Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, open '.../openclaw/dist/package.json'. **Root cause:** `dist/lancedb-runtime-3m75WU-W.js` line 10 reads `package.json` relative to `import.meta.url` (resolves to `dist/`), but the npm package does not include `dist/package.json`. **Workaround:** Manually create `dist/package.json` with `{\\\"dependencies\\\":{\\\"@lancedb/lancedb\\\":\\\"^0.27.1\\\"}}` and re-run `npm install` in `dist/extensions/memory-lancedb/`. **Suggestion:** Include `package.json` (or a minimal version) in `dist/` during build, or fix the path resolution to use the root `package.json`. ## Issue 3: ~40 plugin id mismatch warnings. plugins.entries.anthropic: plugin anthropic: plugin id mismatch (manifest uses \\\"anthropic\\\", entry hints \\\"anthropic-provider\\\"). ## Issue 4: AGENTS.md template missing from npm package. [boot] agent run failed: Missing workspace template: AGENTS.md (.../openclaw/dist/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md). Ensure docs/reference/templates are packaged. **Root cause:** Another build/packaging omission — `dist/docs/reference/templates/` not included in the published npm package. ## Issue 5: openclaw-weixin plugin load failure. openclaw-weixin failed during register: Error: Unable to resolve plugin runtime module. All issues stem from **build/packaging gaps** in v2026.3.24:. 1. Missing `dist/package.json` → lancedb runtime break. 2. Missing `dist/docs/reference/templates/` → boot hook break. 3. In-place dist overwrite during live Gateway → module hash mismatch crash. 4. Plugin id rename without entry hint sync → log noise. No fields configured for issues without a type. ## Issue actions.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d0a34b5f58196055\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9997677\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d00c9d258f231d72\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 · Issue #52885 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d00c9d258f231d72\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52885?timeline_page=1\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b873b2d98f7faf06\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 #52885. 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容#52885. 微信插件 `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` v1.0.3 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22 及更高版本存在兼容性问题。. Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk' Require stack: - C:\\\\Users\\\\Administrator\\\\.openclaw\\\\extensions\\\\openclaw-weixin\\\\index.ts. 1. 微信插件源码 (`index.ts`) 使用 ESM import 从 `openclaw/plugin-sdk` 导入 API：. import{normalizeAccountId} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{stripMarkdown} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{withFileLock} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{resolvePreferredOpenClawTmpDir} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{createTypingCallbacks} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{buildChannelConfigSchema} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\";// ... 2. 但 OpenClaw 的 `dist/plugin-sdk/index.js` 没有导出这些函数（它们只在子模块如 `account-id.js`, `bluebubbles.js`, `file-lock.js` 等中可用）. 3. OpenClaw 最新版本 2026.3.23 的 plugin-sdk 导出的函数：. * OpenClaw 版本：2026.3.22 / 2026.3.23. * Node.js 版本：24.14.0. 请在 OpenClaw 的 `src/plugin-sdk/index.ts` 中添加缺失的导出，或发布一个包含编译后 JS 文件的微信插件版本，使插件可以在不依赖源码解析的情况下工作。. 2. 为插件创建 node\\\\_modules 链接. 3. 使用 NODE\\\\_PATH 环境变量. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b873b2d98f7faf06\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9997131\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d8dc44e0a2f931d2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: openclaw plugins install does not install peer dependency — plugin fails to load after install · Issue #53517 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d8dc44e0a2f931d2\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53517\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"20c983b3e82907ac\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# [Bug]: openclaw plugins install does not install peer dependency — plugin fails to load after install #53517. [[Bug]: openclaw plugins install does not install peer dependency — plugin fails to load after install](#top)#53517. `openclaw plugins install` does not install declared `peerDependencies` into the plugin's `node_modules`, causing the plugin to fail at load time and crash the gateway. 1. Install OpenClaw 2026.3.23-2 globally on Windows. Plugin installs successfully but `openclaw` is not present in `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/node_modules/`. # Plugin declares peer dependency # ~ | \\\"peerDependencies\\\" \\\" \\\" \\\"openclaw\\\" \\\" \\\"\\\">=2026.3.22\\\" \\\" \\\" # But openclaw is missing from plugin's node_modules # ~# Compare with openclaw-lark which works fine # ~# Workaround: manually install the peer dep # cd ~ &&# After this, plugin loads and gateway starts successfully #. * The `openclaw` package is `\\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\"` with exports map including `./plugin-sdk/channel-config-schema` — the file exists at `dist/plugin-sdk/channel-config-schema.js`, resolution fails purely because the package is absent from the plugin's `node_modules`.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"20c983b3e82907ac\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9996947\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57bf6ea1a4923cf5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 · Issue #52885 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57bf6ea1a4923cf5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52885\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba508d2eb9cafbf6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 #52885. 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容#52885. 微信插件 `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` v1.0.3 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22 及更高版本存在兼容性问题。. Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk' Require stack: - C:\\\\Users\\\\Administrator\\\\.openclaw\\\\extensions\\\\openclaw-weixin\\\\index.ts. 1. 微信插件源码 (`index.ts`) 使用 ESM import 从 `openclaw/plugin-sdk` 导入 API：. import{normalizeAccountId} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{stripMarkdown} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{withFileLock} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{resolvePreferredOpenClawTmpDir} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{createTypingCallbacks} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{buildChannelConfigSchema} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\";// ... 2. 但 OpenClaw 的 `dist/plugin-sdk/index.js` 没有导出这些函数（它们只在子模块如 `account-id.js`, `bluebubbles.js`, `file-lock.js` 等中可用）. 3. OpenClaw 最新版本 2026.3.23 的 plugin-sdk 导出的函数：. * OpenClaw 版本：2026.3.22 / 2026.3.23. * Node.js 版本：24.14.0. 请在 OpenClaw 的 `src/plugin-sdk/index.ts` 中添加缺失的导出，或发布一个包含编译后 JS 文件的微信插件版本，使插件可以在不依赖源码解析的情况下工作。. 2. 为插件创建 node\\\\_modules 链接. 3. 使用 NODE\\\\_PATH 环境变量. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba508d2eb9cafbf6\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99962294\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"72de3c78ee3efc27\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages · Issue #52086 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"72de3c78ee3efc27\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52086\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"24e98e96ec09ce4b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. # [openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages #52086. [[openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages](#top)#52086. When a user forwards a WeChat Official Account (公众号) article to the bot, the message is silently dropped — the agent receives nothing. When a link/article message is forwarded, the agent should receive at minimum:. * **Description/summary** (if available from the message payload). * WeChat link messages have type `49` (app message) with sub-types for articles. * The XML payload contains , ,  fields that can be extracted. * Server-side fetching of article content is blocked by WeChat anti-scraping (CAPTCHA), so extracting content on the client side before forwarding would be ideal as a follow-up enhancement. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"24e98e96ec09ce4b\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9996049\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/ weixin openclaw 2026.4.1","provider":"tavily","count":10,"tookMs":2689,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"tavily","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c7ce2226dfe33b97\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 · Issue #52341 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c7ce2226dfe33b97\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52341","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3375503afe158b2a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# [Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 #52341. [[Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14](#top)#52341. After installing `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin@1.0.2` into a local OpenClaw `2026.3.14` source checkout on macOS 26.2, the Weixin plugin does not load consistently: gateway startup logs `Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'` or `Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk/core'`, and CLI plugin loading logs `TypeError: (0 , _pluginSdk.resolvePreferredOpenClawTmpDir) is not a function`. 5. Observe plugin load failures instead of a stable running Weixin channel. After installation and QR login, the external Weixin plugin should load under both gateway startup and CLI/plugin-registry loading, and `channels status` should show a running Weixin account without plugin load errors. * `Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'`. Related existing issue: #52153 is about proactive sending on Weixin; this report is about plugin loading / SDK compatibility before normal runtime behavior. Affected: local/source OpenClaw installs using the external `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` plugin. Consequence: The Weixin plugin does not load reliably, so the channel cannot be used normally.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3375503afe158b2a\">>>","score":0.99989843},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2bdeea3de7927631\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Error running `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp` · Issue #24993 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2bdeea3de7927631\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24993","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8fb44ea9463c8a86\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Error running `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp` · Issue #24993 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Error running `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp` #24993. [[Bug]: Error running `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp`](#top)#24993. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. ## Description. opened on Feb 24, 2026. ### Summary. Running `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp` failed with console error, plugin is not installed. ### Steps to reproduce. openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp. * openclaw: 2026.2.22-2. ### Expected behavior. Expect the plugin to be installed. ### Actual behavior. I see below errors in console:. Downloading @openclaw/whatsapp… npm pack failed: npm notice Access token expired or revoked. Please try logging in again. npm notice Access token expired or revoked. Please try logging in again. npm error code E404 npm error 404 Not Found - GET https://registry.npmjs.org/@openclaw%2fwhatsapp - Not found npm error 404 npm error 404 '@openclaw/whatsapp@*' is not in this registry. npm error 404 npm error 404 Note that you can also install from a npm error 404 tarball, folder, http url, or git url. npm error A complete log of this run can be found in: /Users/xxx/.npm/_logs/2026-02-24T03_04_25_974Z-debug-0.log. ### OpenClaw version. ### Operating system. ### Install method. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. ### Additional information. I've previously ran setup via `openclaw onboard --install-daemon`, during channel setup it also got stuck so I skipped it. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8fb44ea9463c8a86\">>>","score":0.99983776},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e1aa17649d55afe9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIndependent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat · Issue #52537 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e1aa17649d55afe9\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52537","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2647dd2e155be3f7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# Independent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat #52537. Independent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat#52537. Two related issues when using independent agents with the WeChat (openclaw-weixin) channel:. Independent agent does not inherit `agents.defaults.thinkingDefault`. When `thinkingDefault: \"off\"` is set under `agents.defaults`, independent agents (created via `openclaw agents add`) do **not** inherit this setting. New sessions created by inbound messages from the WeChat channel are missing the `reasoning:off` / `think:off` flag. * Main agent session: `reasoning:off` ✅. * Independent wechat agent session: no flag ❌. openclaw-weixin plugin does not filter thinking/reasoning output. The WeChat plugin (`openclaw-weixin`) transparently forwards the full model response to the WeChat chat, including reasoning/thinking blocks. Grep of the weixin plugin source (`src/`) shows zero references to `thinking` or `reasoning` — no filtering logic exists. 1. Independent agents should inherit `agents.defaults.thinkingDefault` (or support per-agent `thinkingDefault` config). 2. The WeChat plugin should strip thinking/reasoning content from outbound messages, consistent with Telegram behavior.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2647dd2e155be3f7\">>>","score":0.9998273},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"979ae33beab3e9ac\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nUser-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23) · Issue #53403 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"979ae33beab3e9ac\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53403","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"38ffe6b959dc2d10\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: User-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23) · Issue #53403 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # User-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23) #53403. User-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23)#53403. * OpenClaw 3.23 (ccfeecb) and 3.23-1. * macOS 15.7.4 x64. * Plugin: `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` 1.0.2 / 1.0.3. * Plugin install path: `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/`. 1. Install OpenClaw 3.23. 2. Install any user plugin that imports from `openclaw/plugin-sdk` (e.g. 3. 3. Start or restart the gateway 4. Plugin fails to load: `Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'`. Bundled plugins (feishu, etc.) work fine — the issue only affects user-installed plugins in `~/.openclaw/extensions/`. ## Root Cause. In `pi-embedded-CwMQzdKD.js`, `loadOpenClawPlugins()` calls `buildPluginLoaderAliasMap(modulePath)` where `modulePath` is the plugin file path (e.g. `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/index.ts`). The jiti-based loader uses this to build an alias map for `openclaw/plugin-sdk*` imports. The alias map builder has two resolution paths:. Finds `root-alias.cjs` by walking **up to 6 levels** from the plugin directory. For `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/`:. 1. ~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/ 2. Never reaches `/usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/` → returns `null`. Calls `resolveLoaderPluginSdkPackageRoot()` → `resolveOpenClawPackageRootSync()` starting from plugin dirname, then `findNearestPluginSdkPackageRoot()` (max 12 levels). Same problem — cannot reach the OpenClaw package root from `~/.openclaw/extensions/`. ### Why it worked in 3.13. In 3.13, the alias for `openclaw/plugin-sdk` (main entry only) used a different resolution strategy that could locate the OpenClaw package. In 3.23, both main entry and subpath resolution fail for user-installed plugins. Bundled plugins work because they are located at `/usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions/` — inside the same package tree. 1. **Search the OpenClaw executable's location** as a candidate root in `resolveLoaderPluginSdkPackageRoot()`. 2. **Set `NODE_PATH`** to include the OpenClaw package parent in the gateway LaunchAgent. 3. **Add a config option** like `plugins.sdkPath` pointing to the OpenClaw installation directory. 4. **Extend the directory walk limit** or use `require.resolve()` to find the OpenClaw package from the gateway process itself. cc @X\\_Corperation (who reported the same issue in the community). ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"38ffe6b959dc2d10\">>>","score":0.9998134},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b616126b34a3ef32\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: local TS extensions importing openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry fail to load on 2026.3.22 · Issue #53002 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b616126b34a3ef32\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53002","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0de54b04a78786f2\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# [Bug]: local TS extensions importing openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry fail to load on 2026.3.22 #53002. [[Bug]: local TS extensions importing openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry fail to load on 2026.3.22](#top)#53002. On OpenClaw 2026.3.22, a local extension under `~/.openclaw/extensions//index.ts` that imports `openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry` fails to load because the plugin loader resolves the import to `.../dist/plugin-sdk/root-alias.cjs/plugin-entry` instead of the scoped subpath target. A local extension using the documented SDK import path `openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry` should load successfully, matching the documented plugin authoring flow and prior observed behavior on earlier versions. [plugins] telegram-album-outbound failed to load from /Users/shinya/.openclaw/extensions/telegram-album-outbound/index.ts: Error: Cannot find module '/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/plugin-sdk/root-alias.cjs/plugin-entry' Require stack: - /Users/shinya/.openclaw/extensions/telegram-album-outbound/index.ts. * In the failing case, `openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry` appears to be resolved via the parent alias and incorrectly expanded to `root-alias.cjs/plugin-entry` instead of `dist/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry.js`. [plugins] telegram-album-outbound failed to load from /Users/shinya/.openclaw/extensions/telegram-album-outbound/index.ts: Error: Cannot find module '/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/plugin-sdk/root-alias.cjs/plugin-entry' Require stack: - /Users/shinya/.openclaw/extensions/telegram-album-outbound/index.ts. * [[Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 #52341](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52341) — external plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 with `Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'`. * Always for the observed local extension using `openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry`.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0de54b04a78786f2\">>>","score":0.9997818},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fa263311bc584bc3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nv2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13 · Issue #54790 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fa263311bc584bc3\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/54790","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d0a34b5f58196055\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: v2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13 · Issue #54790 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. # v2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13 #54790. v2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13#54790. * Install method: `npm install -g openclaw`. * Service management: launchd (`ai.openclaw.gateway`). Upgrading from v2026.3.13 to v2026.3.24 via `openclaw update` caused Gateway crash with multiple packaging/build issues preventing clean restart. ## Issue 1: Gateway crashes during upgrade, launchd fails to auto-restart. **Symptom:** After upgrade, Gateway process terminates. **Root cause:** `npm install -g` overwrites `dist/` in-place while the Gateway is running. [ws] ⇄ res ✗ channels.status 2149ms errorCode=UNAVAILABLE errorMessage=Error: Cannot find module '.../dist/audit-membership-runtime-BT91Am6G.js' imported from '.../dist/reply-Bm8VrLQh.js'. **Workaround:** `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/ai.openclaw.gateway`. **Suggestion:** `openclaw update` should gracefully stop the Gateway before replacing dist files, then restart. ## Issue 2: memory-lancedb plugin fails — `dist/package.json` missing from npm package. [plugins] memory-lancedb failed to load: Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, open '.../openclaw/dist/package.json'. **Root cause:** `dist/lancedb-runtime-3m75WU-W.js` line 10 reads `package.json` relative to `import.meta.url` (resolves to `dist/`), but the npm package does not include `dist/package.json`. **Workaround:** Manually create `dist/package.json` with `{\"dependencies\":{\"@lancedb/lancedb\":\"^0.27.1\"}}` and re-run `npm install` in `dist/extensions/memory-lancedb/`. **Suggestion:** Include `package.json` (or a minimal version) in `dist/` during build, or fix the path resolution to use the root `package.json`. ## Issue 3: ~40 plugin id mismatch warnings. plugins.entries.anthropic: plugin anthropic: plugin id mismatch (manifest uses \"anthropic\", entry hints \"anthropic-provider\"). ## Issue 4: AGENTS.md template missing from npm package. [boot] agent run failed: Missing workspace template: AGENTS.md (.../openclaw/dist/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md). Ensure docs/reference/templates are packaged. **Root cause:** Another build/packaging omission — `dist/docs/reference/templates/` not included in the published npm package. ## Issue 5: openclaw-weixin plugin load failure. openclaw-weixin failed during register: Error: Unable to resolve plugin runtime module. All issues stem from **build/packaging gaps** in v2026.3.24:. 1. Missing `dist/package.json` → lancedb runtime break. 2. Missing `dist/docs/reference/templates/` → boot hook break. 3. In-place dist overwrite during live Gateway → module hash mismatch crash. 4. Plugin id rename without entry hint sync → log noise. No fields configured for issues without a type. ## Issue actions.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d0a34b5f58196055\">>>","score":0.9997677},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d00c9d258f231d72\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 · Issue #52885 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d00c9d258f231d72\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52885?timeline_page=1","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b873b2d98f7faf06\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 #52885. 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容#52885. 微信插件 `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` v1.0.3 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22 及更高版本存在兼容性问题。. Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk' Require stack: - C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.openclaw\\extensions\\openclaw-weixin\\index.ts. 1. 微信插件源码 (`index.ts`) 使用 ESM import 从 `openclaw/plugin-sdk` 导入 API：. import{normalizeAccountId} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{stripMarkdown} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{withFileLock} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{resolvePreferredOpenClawTmpDir} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{createTypingCallbacks} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{buildChannelConfigSchema} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\";// ... 2. 但 OpenClaw 的 `dist/plugin-sdk/index.js` 没有导出这些函数（它们只在子模块如 `account-id.js`, `bluebubbles.js`, `file-lock.js` 等中可用）. 3. OpenClaw 最新版本 2026.3.23 的 plugin-sdk 导出的函数：. * OpenClaw 版本：2026.3.22 / 2026.3.23. * Node.js 版本：24.14.0. 请在 OpenClaw 的 `src/plugin-sdk/index.ts` 中添加缺失的导出，或发布一个包含编译后 JS 文件的微信插件版本，使插件可以在不依赖源码解析的情况下工作。. 2. 为插件创建 node\\_modules 链接. 3. 使用 NODE\\_PATH 环境变量. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b873b2d98f7faf06\">>>","score":0.9997131},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d8dc44e0a2f931d2\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: openclaw plugins install does not install peer dependency — plugin fails to load after install · Issue #53517 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d8dc44e0a2f931d2\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53517","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"20c983b3e82907ac\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# [Bug]: openclaw plugins install does not install peer dependency — plugin fails to load after install #53517. [[Bug]: openclaw plugins install does not install peer dependency — plugin fails to load after install](#top)#53517. `openclaw plugins install` does not install declared `peerDependencies` into the plugin's `node_modules`, causing the plugin to fail at load time and crash the gateway. 1. Install OpenClaw 2026.3.23-2 globally on Windows. Plugin installs successfully but `openclaw` is not present in `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/node_modules/`. # Plugin declares peer dependency # ~ | \"peerDependencies\" \" \" \"openclaw\" \" \"\">=2026.3.22\" \" \" # But openclaw is missing from plugin's node_modules # ~# Compare with openclaw-lark which works fine # ~# Workaround: manually install the peer dep # cd ~ &&# After this, plugin loads and gateway starts successfully #. * The `openclaw` package is `\"type\": \"module\"` with exports map including `./plugin-sdk/channel-config-schema` — the file exists at `dist/plugin-sdk/channel-config-schema.js`, resolution fails purely because the package is absent from the plugin's `node_modules`.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"20c983b3e82907ac\">>>","score":0.9996947},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"57bf6ea1a4923cf5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 · Issue #52885 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"57bf6ea1a4923cf5\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52885","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ba508d2eb9cafbf6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 #52885. 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容#52885. 微信插件 `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` v1.0.3 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22 及更高版本存在兼容性问题。. Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk' Require stack: - C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.openclaw\\extensions\\openclaw-weixin\\index.ts. 1. 微信插件源码 (`index.ts`) 使用 ESM import 从 `openclaw/plugin-sdk` 导入 API：. import{normalizeAccountId} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{stripMarkdown} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{withFileLock} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{resolvePreferredOpenClawTmpDir} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{createTypingCallbacks} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{buildChannelConfigSchema} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\";// ... 2. 但 OpenClaw 的 `dist/plugin-sdk/index.js` 没有导出这些函数（它们只在子模块如 `account-id.js`, `bluebubbles.js`, `file-lock.js` 等中可用）. 3. OpenClaw 最新版本 2026.3.23 的 plugin-sdk 导出的函数：. * OpenClaw 版本：2026.3.22 / 2026.3.23. * Node.js 版本：24.14.0. 请在 OpenClaw 的 `src/plugin-sdk/index.ts` 中添加缺失的导出，或发布一个包含编译后 JS 文件的微信插件版本，使插件可以在不依赖源码解析的情况下工作。. 2. 为插件创建 node\\_modules 链接. 3. 使用 NODE\\_PATH 环境变量. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ba508d2eb9cafbf6\">>>","score":0.99962294},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"72de3c78ee3efc27\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages · Issue #52086 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"72de3c78ee3efc27\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52086","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"24e98e96ec09ce4b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. # [openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages #52086. [[openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages](#top)#52086. When a user forwards a WeChat Official Account (公众号) article to the bot, the message is silently dropped — the agent receives nothing. When a link/article message is forwarded, the agent should receive at minimum:. * **Description/summary** (if available from the message payload). * WeChat link messages have type `49` (app message) with sub-types for articles. * The XML payload contains , ,  fields that can be extracted. * Server-side fetching of article content is blocked by WeChat anti-scraping (CAPTCHA), so extracting content on the client side before forwarding would be ideal as a follow-up enhancement. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"24e98e96ec09ce4b\">>>","score":0.9996049}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775088283728}}
{"type":"message","id":"cf418f8c","parentId":"89922280","timestamp":"2026-04-02T00:04:44.189Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_89DB304C7GMS4mnqh3TQhAOc|fc_063f6e7d06c593d70169cdb298b0e8819194f2eb28a4057b74","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/ Discord help bug openclaw \\\"2026.4.1\\\"\",\n  \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 3109,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6b337393acc2ea8b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Bug Report: Discord typing indicator persists after bot reply · Issue #26260 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6b337393acc2ea8b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/26260\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0061706deb2fd46b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Bug]: Bug Report: Discord typing indicator persists after bot reply · Issue #26260 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Bug Report: Discord typing indicator persists after bot reply #26260. [[Bug]: Bug Report: Discord typing indicator persists after bot reply](#top)#26260. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. ## Description. opened on Feb 25, 2026. ### Summary. ### Description. After the bot successfully sends a reply in Discord, the \\\"typing indicator\\\" (\\\"Bot is typing...\\\") continues to display indefinitely instead of dismissing after the message is sent. ### Relevant Config. ### Steps to reproduce. 1. Configure OpenClaw with Discord channel integration. 2. Mention the bot or send a message that triggers a response. 3. Bot sends a complete reply successfully. 4. Observe that the typing indicator remains visible below the message. ### Expected behavior. The typing indicator should be dismissed immediately after the bot finishes sending its reply. ### Actual behavior. The typing indicator persists after the reply is delivered. It does not clear automatically in a timely manner, even with `streaming` set to `off` in the Discord channel config. \\\"channels\\\" \\\"discord\\\" \\\"enabled\\\" true \\\"streaming\\\" \\\"off\\\" \\\" \\\". ### OpenClaw version. OpenClaw Version: 2026.2.24. ### Operating system. ### Install method. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. ### Additional information. This appears to be a cosmetic issue where `sendTyping()` is being called without a corresponding cancellation after the message is sent. The typing indicator eventually disappears on its own after ~10 seconds, but it reappears continuously as long as the bot is active, suggesting the typing signal may be looping. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0061706deb2fd46b\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9999963\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b85b29aff960527e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Discord Application ID Precision Loss · Issue #29608 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b85b29aff960527e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/29608\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ea75ba280b8ca38d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Bug]: Discord Application ID Precision Loss · Issue #29608 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Discord Application ID Precision Loss #29608. [[Bug]: Discord Application ID Precision Loss](#top)#29608. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. ## Description. opened on Feb 28, 2026. ### Summary. ## Summary. OpenClaw fails to resolve Discord Application IDs that exceed JavaScript's Number.MAX\\\\_SAFE\\\\_INTEGER (2^53 - 1), resulting in \\\"Failed to resolve Discord application id\\\" errors even with valid bot tokens. ## Version. * OpenClaw: 2026.2.26 (bc50708). * Platform: macOS (Darwin 23.5.0). ## Description. Discord Application IDs are 64-bit integers that can exceed JavaScript's safe integer range. When OpenClaw parses the bot token to extract the Application ID, it appears to use `Number` type instead of `BigInt` or string, causing precision loss for IDs >= 2^53. ### Steps to reproduce. 1. Create a Discord application with Application ID: `1477179610322964541` (19 digits). 2. Generate a bot token from Discord Developer Portal. 3. Configure OpenClaw with the bot token:. \\\"channels\\\" \\\"discord\\\" \\\"enabled\\\" true \\\"token\\\"\\\"MTQ3NzE3OTYxMDMyMjk2NDU0MQ.GhIiP9.vU1xEpJ6NjFm-a7Ra_9pEZzdxQ7GQOLpiM0PzI\\\" \\\" \\\". 5. Check logs: `tail -f ~/.openclaw/logs/gateway.err.log`. ### Expected behavior. * No \\\"Failed to resolve Discord application id\\\" errors. ### Actual behavior. [discord] [default] channel exited: Failed to resolve Discord application id. Repeated every few seconds with auto-retry attempts. ### OpenClaw version. ### Operating system. ### Install method. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. ## Suggested Fix. Update Discord token parsing to use `BigInt` or preserve as string:. // Current (buggy) const appId = Number(Buffer. toString())// Fixed option 1: Use BigInt const appId = BigInt('0x' + Buffer. toString('hex'))// Fixed option 2: Keep as string const appId = Buffer. ## Workaround. Currently no known workaround within configuration. 1. Use a Discord application with ID < 2^53 (unlikely for newer applications). 2. Wait for OpenClaw fix. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ea75ba280b8ca38d\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9999906\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"749302efd6356e8a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Discord Plugin Bug Report - Real-time Message Receiving Broken · Issue #13561 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"749302efd6356e8a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/13561\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4d22bd9dac374c47\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nYou signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. # [Bug]: Discord Plugin Bug Report - Real-time Message Receiving Broken #13561. [[Bug]: Discord Plugin Bug Report - Real-time Message Receiving Broken](#top)#13561. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. Discord plugin can **send** messages and **poll** messages via REST API, but **real-time websocket receiving is broken**. Messages from users only appear when manually checking, not as live events. ✅ Bot invited to server with Send Messages permission. ### What WORKS:. * Sending messages via `message tool` (REST API). * Polling messages via `message action=read` (REST API). * Real-time websocket/gateway message receiving. * Messages sent by users do NOT trigger instant agent responses. 2. Enable Message Content Intent in Discord Developer Portal. 3. Send message from Discord client. 4. Observe: Agent does NOT receive real-time notification. Agent should receive real-time websocket events when users send messages in Discord. Cannot use Discord for real-time mobile communication. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4d22bd9dac374c47\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99998\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6da3317f0e40dcf0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Discord MESSAGE_CREATE events not received on macOS (v2026.2.14) · Issue #17597 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6da3317f0e40dcf0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/17597\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c5736726f8b4cd59\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Bug]: Discord MESSAGE_CREATE events not received on macOS (v2026.2.14) · Issue #17597 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Discord MESSAGE\\\\_CREATE events not received on macOS (v2026.2.14) #17597. [[Bug]: Discord MESSAGE\\\\_CREATE events not received on macOS (v2026.2.14)](#top)#17597. ## Description. opened on Feb 15, 2026. ### Environment. * **OpenClaw Version**: 2026.2.14. * **Node.js Version**: 22.22.0. * **OS**: macOS 26.2 (Darwin 25.2.0 arm64). ### Description. The Discord bot connects successfully, logs in, and resolves the guild. It appears online with Administrator permissions. However, regular messages (MESSAGE\\\\_CREATE events) are never received or logged by the gateway, even with `diagnostics.flags: [\\\"discord.*\\\"]\\\\ outdoor` enabled. This appears to be related to or the same as #16860 and #4555. ### Steps Taken / Diagnostics. 1. **Permissions**: Bot has Administrator permissions and is added to the server. 2. **Config**: `groupPolicy` is set to `allowlist` and the guild ID is correctly whitelisted. 3. **Doctor**: Ran `openclaw doctor --fix` which cleaned up some stale `dm.policy` fields, but did not fix the message receipt. * `[discord] logged in to discord as ...` (Success). * `[discord] channels resolved: guild:...` (Success). * Zero inbound messages logged when sending @mentions or regular text in whitelisted channels. 5. **Restarts**: Tried both SIGUSR1 (config reload) and full process stop/start. ### Logs. 2026-02-15T23:29:36.887Z [discord] [default] Discord Message Content Intent is limited; bots under 100 servers can use it without verification. 2026-02-15T23:29:36.889Z [discord] [default] starting provider (@Moon) 2026-02-15T23:29:37.101Z [discord] channels resolved: guild:865909145433276446→865909145433276446 2026-02-15T23:29:37.712Z [discord] logged in to discord as 1472604324096901263. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c5736726f8b4cd59\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9999776\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"97ab8b822319b372\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Discord Plugin unavailable during fresh install · Issue #24781 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"97ab8b822319b372\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24781\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b501881a7d64a096\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: 