es/27851\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aedad2ce421996a8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Bug]:Discord EventQueue timeout (30s) too aggressive for AI responses · Issue #27851 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n# [Bug]:Discord EventQueue timeout (30s) too aggressive for AI responses #27851. [[Bug]:Discord EventQueue timeout (30s) too aggressive for AI responses](#top)#27851. # OpenClaw Discord EventQueue Timeout Bug Report. Discord listener consistently times out after 30 seconds, causing the bot to stop responding to messages. The Discord EventQueue has a hardcoded 30-second timeout that is too aggressive for AI responses. [EventQueue] Listener DiscordMessageListener timed out after 30000ms for event MESSAGE_CREATE {\\\"subsystem\\\":\\\"discord/monitor\\\"} Slow listener detected: 224.2 seconds {\\\"subsystem\\\":\\\"agent/embedded\\\"} embedded run done: durationMs: 222127 aborted=false. * Discord listener timed out after only 30 seconds. 1. **Make timeout configurable** - Allow users to set `discord.eventQueue.timeout` in config. **Would love to see a fix for this — it's the biggest stability issue with OpenClaw + Discord right now.**. # OpenClaw Discord EventQueue Timeout Bug Report. Discord listener consistently times out after 30 seconds, causing the bot to stop responding to messages. The Discord EventQueue has a hardcoded 30-second timeout that is too aggressive for AI responses. [EventQueue] Listener DiscordMessageListener timed out after 30000ms for event MESSAGE_CREATE {\\\"subsystem\\\":\\\"discord/monitor\\\"} Slow listener detected: 224.2 seconds {\\\"subsystem\\\":\\\"agent/embedded\\\"} embedded run done: durationMs: 222127 aborted=false. * Discord listener timed out after only 30 seconds. 1. **Make timeout configurable** - Allow users to set `discord.eventQueue.timeout` in config. # OpenClaw Discord EventQueue Timeout Bug Report. Discord listener consistently times out after 30 seconds, causing the bot to stop responding to messages. The Discord EventQueue has a hardcoded 30-second timeout that is too aggressive for AI responses. [EventQueue] Listener DiscordMessageListener timed out after 30000ms for event MESSAGE_CREATE {\\\"subsystem\\\":\\\"discord/monitor\\\"} Slow listener detected: 224.2 seconds {\\\"subsystem\\\":\\\"agent/embedded\\\"} embedded run done: durationMs: 222127 aborted=false. * Discord listener timed out after only 30 seconds. 1. **Make timeout configurable** - Allow users to set `discord.eventQueue.timeout` in config. # OpenClaw Discord EventQueue Timeout Bug Report. Discord listener consistently times out after 30 seconds, causing the bot to stop responding to messages. The Discord EventQueue has a hardcoded 30-second timeout that is too aggressive for AI responses. [EventQueue] Listener DiscordMessageListener timed out after 30000ms for event MESSAGE_CREATE {\\\"subsystem\\\":\\\"discord/monitor\\\"} Slow listener detected: 224.2 seconds {\\\"subsystem\\\":\\\"agent/embedded\\\"} embedded run done: durationMs: 222127 aborted=false. * Discord listener timed out after only 30 seconds. 1. **Make timeout configurable** - Allow users to set `discord.eventQueue.timeout` in config.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aedad2ce421996a8\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9999685\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5175c94a7535cf5a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Discord thread mentions not working · Issue #44183 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5175c94a7535cf5a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/44183\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0a1d9af1afb3294e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Bug]: Discord thread mentions not working · Issue #44183 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Discord thread mentions not working #44183. [[Bug]: Discord thread mentions not working](#top)#44183. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingbug:behaviorIncorrect behavior without a crashIncorrect behavior without a crash. ## Description. opened on Mar 12, 2026. ### Bug type. Behavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash). ### Summary. 1. ✅ **原始线程** (channel:1481592486802489385) → 能正常响应. 2. ❌ **频道主区** (channel:1481591534468989181) → 日志显示 `no-mention`，无响应. 3. ❌ **新线程** (channel:1481663889845256284) → 日志显示 `no-mention`，无响应. ### Steps to reproduce. 3. Bot 没有响应，日志显示 `no-mention`. ### Expected behavior. ### Actual behavior. ### OpenClaw version. ### Operating system. ### Install method. ### Model. ### Provider / routing chain. ### Config file / key location. ### Additional provider/model setup details. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. ### Additional information. * PR feat(slack): add allowBots \\\"mentions\\\" mode (parity with Discord) #43588: add allowBots \\\"mentions\\\" mode (parity with Discord). * Issue [[Feature]: Slack allowBots: \\\"mentions\\\" mode (parity with Discord) #43587](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/43587): [Feature]: Slack allowBots: \\\"mentions\\\" mode. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingbug:behaviorIncorrect behavior without a crashIncorrect behavior without a crash. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0a1d9af1afb3294e\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9999417\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b4a3a8fe753c277d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: 🐛 OpenClaw Discord Channel Login Failure Report · Issue #17080 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b4a3a8fe753c277d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/17080\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ab0ce8a004ea5fdb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Bug]: 🐛 OpenClaw Discord Channel Login Failure Report · Issue #17080 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... # [Bug]: 🐛 OpenClaw Discord Channel Login Failure Report #17080. [[Bug]: 🐛 OpenClaw Discord Channel Login Failure Report](#top)#17080. 🐛 OpenClaw Discord Channel Login Failure Report. OpenClaw Version: 2026.2.14 (installed via npm). Installation Method: npm install -g openclaw. When configuring the Discord channel with a valid Discord Bot Token, the OpenClaw gateway consistently fails to log in with the error:. [discord] [default] channel exited: Failed to resolve Discord application id. However, the same token works perfectly when tested with curl, returning the correct bot information. Deleted ~/.openclaw/credentials/discord-\\\\*.json. Deleted ~/.openclaw/channels/discord\\\\* (if existed). Deleted ~/.openclaw/providers/discord\\\\* (if existed). Confirmed with env | grep DISCORD\\\\_TOKEN that the variable was correctly set. Created ~/.openclaw/credentials/discord.json with:. 11:02:33 [discord] [default] channel exited: Failed to resolve Discord application id. DEBUG logs contained no further Discord-related error output (only mDNS and ciao service debug information). The same token works normally in other bot frameworks (e.g., discord.py). All installed skills (like youtube-watcher) work fine when called from the command line, indicating the core OpenClaw functionality is normal. Why can OpenClaw not resolve the Discord application ID using this valid token? Deleted ~/.openclaw/credentials/discord-\\\\*.json. Deleted ~/.openclaw/channels/discord\\\\* (if existed). Deleted ~/.openclaw/providers/discord\\\\* (if existed). Confirmed with env | grep DISCORD\\\\_TOKEN that the variable was correctly set. Created ~/.openclaw/credentials/discord.json with:. 11:02:33 [discord] [default] channel exited: Failed to resolve Discord application id. DEBUG logs contained no further Discord-related error output (only mDNS and ciao service debug information). ciao:CiaoService [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw)] Rebuilding service records... ciao:Prober Starting to probe for 'VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\\\_openclaw-gw.\\\\_tcp.local.'... ciao:Prober Sending prober query number 1 for 'VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\\\_openclaw-gw.\\\\_tcp.local.'... 😢11:04:37 [discord] [default] channel exited: Failed to resolve Discord application id. ciao:Prober Sending prober query number 2 for 'VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\\\_openclaw-gw.\\\\_tcp.local.'... ciao:Prober Sending prober query number 3 for 'VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\\\_openclaw-gw.\\\\_tcp.local.'... ciao:Prober Probing for 'VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\\\_openclaw-gw.\\\\_tcp.local.' finished successfully +251ms. ciao:Announcer [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\\\_openclaw-gw.\\\\_tcp.local.] Sending announcement for service +0ms. ciao:CiaoService [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw)] Rebuilding service records... ciao:Announcer [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\\\_openclaw-gw.\\\\_tcp.local.] Sending announcement number 1 +3ms. ciao:Announcer [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\\\_openclaw-gw.\\\\_tcp.local.] Sending announcement number 2 +1s. ciao:Announcer [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\\\_openclaw-gw.\\\\_tcp.local.] Sending announcement number 3 +2s. ciao:Responder [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\\\_openclaw-gw.\\\\_tcp.local.] Removing service from the network +3m. ciao:Announcer [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\\\_openclaw-gw.\\\\_tcp.local.] Sending goodbye for service +3m. ciao:Announcer [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\\\_openclaw-gw.\\\\_tcp.local.] Sending goodbye number 1 +5ms. ### OpenClaw version.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ab0ce8a004ea5fdb\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9999263\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"35b34a6fe482eefb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Discord Plugin unavailable during fresh install · Issue #24781 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"35b34a6fe482eefb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24806/linked_closing_reference?reference_location=REPO_ISSUES_INDEX\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ef59f929393b81b3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Bug]: Discord Plugin unavailable during fresh install · Issue #24781 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Discord Plugin unavailable during fresh install #24781. [[Bug]: Discord Plugin unavailable during fresh install](#top)#24781. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. ## Description. opened on Feb 23, 2026. ### Summary. During a fresh VPS install, selecting Discord (BOT API) under channel selection fails to install. ### Steps to reproduce. 1. Fresh Debian 13 install on VPS. 2. Run curl -fsSL  | sh. 3. Setup via guided onboarding. 4. Get to Channel Selection step. 6. Input Discord Bot API key. 7. See Channel Setup: \\\"discord plugin not available.\\\". ### Expected behavior. 1. Input discord API key. 2. Continue with discord setup. ### Actual behavior. ### OpenClaw version. ### Operating system. ### Install method. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. ### Additional information. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ef59f929393b81b3\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99991655\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bfc0143b6a6165ca\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Discord plugin fails with \\\"fetch failed\\\" when using proxy · Issue #42702 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bfc0143b6a6165ca\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/42702\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8b1b4cebf02a8b99\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nYou signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. # [Bug]: Discord plugin fails with \\\"fetch failed\\\" when using proxy #42702. [[Bug]: Discord plugin fails with \\\"fetch failed\\\" when using proxy](#top)#42702. Discord plugin shows `ON | OK` but health check shows `fetch failed`. Proxy setting (`channels.discord.proxy`) not applied to REST API calls. 1. Configure `channels.discord.proxy` in OpenClaw config. 3. Verify proxy works: `curl -x $PROXY https://discord.com/api/...` ✅. 4. Run `openclaw message send --channel=discord ...`. ### Expected behavior. When `channels.discord.proxy` is configured, all Discord HTTP requests (REST. API + WebSocket) should route through the proxy. * `channels.discord.proxy` is only applied to WebSocket connections, not. + `openclaw status` shows `ON | OK` for Discord plugin, but health check. + `openclaw message send --channel=discord` times out or fails with `fetch failed` in proxy-required environments. `openclaw-tui` (CLI) → OpenClaw Gateway → `discord` channel (via `channels.discord.proxy`). ### Additional provider/model setup details. No fields configured for issues without a type.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8b1b4cebf02a8b99\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99990237\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/ Discord help bug openclaw \"2026.4.1\"","provider":"tavily","count":10,"tookMs":3109,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"tavily","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6b337393acc2ea8b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Bug Report: Discord typing indicator persists after bot reply · Issue #26260 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6b337393acc2ea8b\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/26260","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0061706deb2fd46b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Bug Report: Discord typing indicator persists after bot reply · Issue #26260 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Bug Report: Discord typing indicator persists after bot reply #26260. [[Bug]: Bug Report: Discord typing indicator persists after bot reply](#top)#26260. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. ## Description. opened on Feb 25, 2026. ### Summary. ### Description. After the bot successfully sends a reply in Discord, the \"typing indicator\" (\"Bot is typing...\") continues to display indefinitely instead of dismissing after the message is sent. ### Relevant Config. ### Steps to reproduce. 1. Configure OpenClaw with Discord channel integration. 2. Mention the bot or send a message that triggers a response. 3. Bot sends a complete reply successfully. 4. Observe that the typing indicator remains visible below the message. ### Expected behavior. The typing indicator should be dismissed immediately after the bot finishes sending its reply. ### Actual behavior. The typing indicator persists after the reply is delivered. It does not clear automatically in a timely manner, even with `streaming` set to `off` in the Discord channel config. \"channels\" \"discord\" \"enabled\" true \"streaming\" \"off\" \" \". ### OpenClaw version. OpenClaw Version: 2026.2.24. ### Operating system. ### Install method. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. ### Additional information. This appears to be a cosmetic issue where `sendTyping()` is being called without a corresponding cancellation after the message is sent. The typing indicator eventually disappears on its own after ~10 seconds, but it reappears continuously as long as the bot is active, suggesting the typing signal may be looping. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0061706deb2fd46b\">>>","score":0.9999963},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b85b29aff960527e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Discord Application ID Precision Loss · Issue #29608 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b85b29aff960527e\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/29608","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ea75ba280b8ca38d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Discord Application ID Precision Loss · Issue #29608 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Discord Application ID Precision Loss #29608. [[Bug]: Discord Application ID Precision Loss](#top)#29608. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. ## Description. opened on Feb 28, 2026. ### Summary. ## Summary. OpenClaw fails to resolve Discord Application IDs that exceed JavaScript's Number.MAX\\_SAFE\\_INTEGER (2^53 - 1), resulting in \"Failed to resolve Discord application id\" errors even with valid bot tokens. ## Version. * OpenClaw: 2026.2.26 (bc50708). * Platform: macOS (Darwin 23.5.0). ## Description. Discord Application IDs are 64-bit integers that can exceed JavaScript's safe integer range. When OpenClaw parses the bot token to extract the Application ID, it appears to use `Number` type instead of `BigInt` or string, causing precision loss for IDs >= 2^53. ### Steps to reproduce. 1. Create a Discord application with Application ID: `1477179610322964541` (19 digits). 2. Generate a bot token from Discord Developer Portal. 3. Configure OpenClaw with the bot token:. \"channels\" \"discord\" \"enabled\" true \"token\"\"MTQ3NzE3OTYxMDMyMjk2NDU0MQ.GhIiP9.vU1xEpJ6NjFm-a7Ra_9pEZzdxQ7GQOLpiM0PzI\" \" \". 5. Check logs: `tail -f ~/.openclaw/logs/gateway.err.log`. ### Expected behavior. * No \"Failed to resolve Discord application id\" errors. ### Actual behavior. [discord] [default] channel exited: Failed to resolve Discord application id. Repeated every few seconds with auto-retry attempts. ### OpenClaw version. ### Operating system. ### Install method. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. ## Suggested Fix. Update Discord token parsing to use `BigInt` or preserve as string:. // Current (buggy) const appId = Number(Buffer. toString())// Fixed option 1: Use BigInt const appId = BigInt('0x' + Buffer. toString('hex'))// Fixed option 2: Keep as string const appId = Buffer. ## Workaround. Currently no known workaround within configuration. 1. Use a Discord application with ID < 2^53 (unlikely for newer applications). 2. Wait for OpenClaw fix. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ea75ba280b8ca38d\">>>","score":0.9999906},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"749302efd6356e8a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Discord Plugin Bug Report - Real-time Message Receiving Broken · Issue #13561 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"749302efd6356e8a\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/13561","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4d22bd9dac374c47\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nYou signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. # [Bug]: Discord Plugin Bug Report - Real-time Message Receiving Broken #13561. [[Bug]: Discord Plugin Bug Report - Real-time Message Receiving Broken](#top)#13561. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. Discord plugin can **send** messages and **poll** messages via REST API, but **real-time websocket receiving is broken**. Messages from users only appear when manually checking, not as live events. ✅ Bot invited to server with Send Messages permission. ### What WORKS:. * Sending messages via `message tool` (REST API). * Polling messages via `message action=read` (REST API). * Real-time websocket/gateway message receiving. * Messages sent by users do NOT trigger instant agent responses. 2. Enable Message Content Intent in Discord Developer Portal. 3. Send message from Discord client. 4. Observe: Agent does NOT receive real-time notification. Agent should receive real-time websocket events when users send messages in Discord. Cannot use Discord for real-time mobile communication. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4d22bd9dac374c47\">>>","score":0.99998},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6da3317f0e40dcf0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Discord MESSAGE_CREATE events not received on macOS (v2026.2.14) · Issue #17597 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6da3317f0e40dcf0\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/17597","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c5736726f8b4cd59\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Discord MESSAGE_CREATE events not received on macOS (v2026.2.14) · Issue #17597 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Discord MESSAGE\\_CREATE events not received on macOS (v2026.2.14) #17597. [[Bug]: Discord MESSAGE\\_CREATE events not received on macOS (v2026.2.14)](#top)#17597. ## Description. opened on Feb 15, 2026. ### Environment. * **OpenClaw Version**: 2026.2.14. * **Node.js Version**: 22.22.0. * **OS**: macOS 26.2 (Darwin 25.2.0 arm64). ### Description. The Discord bot connects successfully, logs in, and resolves the guild. It appears online with Administrator permissions. However, regular messages (MESSAGE\\_CREATE events) are never received or logged by the gateway, even with `diagnostics.flags: [\"discord.*\"]\\ outdoor` enabled. This appears to be related to or the same as #16860 and #4555. ### Steps Taken / Diagnostics. 1. **Permissions**: Bot has Administrator permissions and is added to the server. 2. **Config**: `groupPolicy` is set to `allowlist` and the guild ID is correctly whitelisted. 3. **Doctor**: Ran `openclaw doctor --fix` which cleaned up some stale `dm.policy` fields, but did not fix the message receipt. * `[discord] logged in to discord as ...` (Success). * `[discord] channels resolved: guild:...` (Success). * Zero inbound messages logged when sending @mentions or regular text in whitelisted channels. 5. **Restarts**: Tried both SIGUSR1 (config reload) and full process stop/start. ### Logs. 2026-02-15T23:29:36.887Z [discord] [default] Discord Message Content Intent is limited; bots under 100 servers can use it without verification. 2026-02-15T23:29:36.889Z [discord] [default] starting provider (@Moon) 2026-02-15T23:29:37.101Z [discord] channels resolved: guild:865909145433276446→865909145433276446 2026-02-15T23:29:37.712Z [discord] logged in to discord as 1472604324096901263. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c5736726f8b4cd59\">>>","score":0.9999776},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"97ab8b822319b372\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Discord Plugin unavailable during fresh install · Issue #24781 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"97ab8b822319b372\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24781","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b501881a7d64a096\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Discord Plugin unavailable during fresh install · Issue #24781 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Discord Plugin unavailable during fresh install #24781. [[Bug]: Discord Plugin unavailable during fresh install](#top)#24