ms for event MESSAGE_CREATE {\"subsystem\":\"discord/monitor\"} Slow listener detected: 224.2 seconds {\"subsystem\":\"agent/embedded\"} embedded run done: durationMs: 222127 aborted=false. * Discord listener timed out after only 30 seconds. 1. **Make timeout configurable** - Allow users to set `discord.eventQueue.timeout` in config. **Would love to see a fix for this — it's the biggest stability issue with OpenClaw + Discord right now.**. # OpenClaw Discord EventQueue Timeout Bug Report. Discord listener consistently times out after 30 seconds, causing the bot to stop responding to messages. The Discord EventQueue has a hardcoded 30-second timeout that is too aggressive for AI responses. [EventQueue] Listener DiscordMessageListener timed out after 30000ms for event MESSAGE_CREATE {\"subsystem\":\"discord/monitor\"} Slow listener detected: 224.2 seconds {\"subsystem\":\"agent/embedded\"} embedded run done: durationMs: 222127 aborted=false. * Discord listener timed out after only 30 seconds. 1. **Make timeout configurable** - Allow users to set `discord.eventQueue.timeout` in config. # OpenClaw Discord EventQueue Timeout Bug Report. Discord listener consistently times out after 30 seconds, causing the bot to stop responding to messages. The Discord EventQueue has a hardcoded 30-second timeout that is too aggressive for AI responses. [EventQueue] Listener DiscordMessageListener timed out after 30000ms for event MESSAGE_CREATE {\"subsystem\":\"discord/monitor\"} Slow listener detected: 224.2 seconds {\"subsystem\":\"agent/embedded\"} embedded run done: durationMs: 222127 aborted=false. * Discord listener timed out after only 30 seconds. 1. **Make timeout configurable** - Allow users to set `discord.eventQueue.timeout` in config. # OpenClaw Discord EventQueue Timeout Bug Report. Discord listener consistently times out after 30 seconds, causing the bot to stop responding to messages. The Discord EventQueue has a hardcoded 30-second timeout that is too aggressive for AI responses. [EventQueue] Listener DiscordMessageListener timed out after 30000ms for event MESSAGE_CREATE {\"subsystem\":\"discord/monitor\"} Slow listener detected: 224.2 seconds {\"subsystem\":\"agent/embedded\"} embedded run done: durationMs: 222127 aborted=false. * Discord listener timed out after only 30 seconds. 1. **Make timeout configurable** - Allow users to set `discord.eventQueue.timeout` in config.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"aedad2ce421996a8\">>>","score":0.9999685},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5175c94a7535cf5a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Discord thread mentions not working · Issue #44183 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5175c94a7535cf5a\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/44183","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0a1d9af1afb3294e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Discord thread mentions not working · Issue #44183 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Discord thread mentions not working #44183. [[Bug]: Discord thread mentions not working](#top)#44183. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingbug:behaviorIncorrect behavior without a crashIncorrect behavior without a crash. ## Description. opened on Mar 12, 2026. ### Bug type. Behavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash). ### Summary. 1. ✅ **原始线程** (channel:1481592486802489385) → 能正常响应. 2. ❌ **频道主区** (channel:1481591534468989181) → 日志显示 `no-mention`，无响应. 3. ❌ **新线程** (channel:1481663889845256284) → 日志显示 `no-mention`，无响应. ### Steps to reproduce. 3. Bot 没有响应，日志显示 `no-mention`. ### Expected behavior. ### Actual behavior. ### OpenClaw version. ### Operating system. ### Install method. ### Model. ### Provider / routing chain. ### Config file / key location. ### Additional provider/model setup details. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. ### Additional information. * PR feat(slack): add allowBots \"mentions\" mode (parity with Discord) #43588: add allowBots \"mentions\" mode (parity with Discord). * Issue [[Feature]: Slack allowBots: \"mentions\" mode (parity with Discord) #43587](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/43587): [Feature]: Slack allowBots: \"mentions\" mode. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingbug:behaviorIncorrect behavior without a crashIncorrect behavior without a crash. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0a1d9af1afb3294e\">>>","score":0.9999417},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b4a3a8fe753c277d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: 🐛 OpenClaw Discord Channel Login Failure Report · Issue #17080 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b4a3a8fe753c277d\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/17080","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ab0ce8a004ea5fdb\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: 🐛 OpenClaw Discord Channel Login Failure Report · Issue #17080 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... # [Bug]: 🐛 OpenClaw Discord Channel Login Failure Report #17080. [[Bug]: 🐛 OpenClaw Discord Channel Login Failure Report](#top)#17080. 🐛 OpenClaw Discord Channel Login Failure Report. OpenClaw Version: 2026.2.14 (installed via npm). Installation Method: npm install -g openclaw. When configuring the Discord channel with a valid Discord Bot Token, the OpenClaw gateway consistently fails to log in with the error:. [discord] [default] channel exited: Failed to resolve Discord application id. However, the same token works perfectly when tested with curl, returning the correct bot information. Deleted ~/.openclaw/credentials/discord-\\*.json. Deleted ~/.openclaw/channels/discord\\* (if existed). Deleted ~/.openclaw/providers/discord\\* (if existed). Confirmed with env | grep DISCORD\\_TOKEN that the variable was correctly set. Created ~/.openclaw/credentials/discord.json with:. 11:02:33 [discord] [default] channel exited: Failed to resolve Discord application id. DEBUG logs contained no further Discord-related error output (only mDNS and ciao service debug information). The same token works normally in other bot frameworks (e.g., discord.py). All installed skills (like youtube-watcher) work fine when called from the command line, indicating the core OpenClaw functionality is normal. Why can OpenClaw not resolve the Discord application ID using this valid token? Deleted ~/.openclaw/credentials/discord-\\*.json. Deleted ~/.openclaw/channels/discord\\* (if existed). Deleted ~/.openclaw/providers/discord\\* (if existed). Confirmed with env | grep DISCORD\\_TOKEN that the variable was correctly set. Created ~/.openclaw/credentials/discord.json with:. 11:02:33 [discord] [default] channel exited: Failed to resolve Discord application id. DEBUG logs contained no further Discord-related error output (only mDNS and ciao service debug information). ciao:CiaoService [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw)] Rebuilding service records... ciao:Prober Starting to probe for 'VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\_openclaw-gw.\\_tcp.local.'... ciao:Prober Sending prober query number 1 for 'VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\_openclaw-gw.\\_tcp.local.'... 😢11:04:37 [discord] [default] channel exited: Failed to resolve Discord application id. ciao:Prober Sending prober query number 2 for 'VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\_openclaw-gw.\\_tcp.local.'... ciao:Prober Sending prober query number 3 for 'VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\_openclaw-gw.\\_tcp.local.'... ciao:Prober Probing for 'VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\_openclaw-gw.\\_tcp.local.' finished successfully +251ms. ciao:Announcer [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\_openclaw-gw.\\_tcp.local.] Sending announcement for service +0ms. ciao:CiaoService [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw)] Rebuilding service records... ciao:Announcer [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\_openclaw-gw.\\_tcp.local.] Sending announcement number 1 +3ms. ciao:Announcer [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\_openclaw-gw.\\_tcp.local.] Sending announcement number 2 +1s. ciao:Announcer [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\_openclaw-gw.\\_tcp.local.] Sending announcement number 3 +2s. ciao:Responder [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\_openclaw-gw.\\_tcp.local.] Removing service from the network +3m. ciao:Announcer [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\_openclaw-gw.\\_tcp.local.] Sending goodbye for service +3m. ciao:Announcer [VM-0-10-opencloudos (OpenClaw).\\_openclaw-gw.\\_tcp.local.] Sending goodbye number 1 +5ms. ### OpenClaw version.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ab0ce8a004ea5fdb\">>>","score":0.9999263},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"35b34a6fe482eefb\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Discord Plugin unavailable during fresh install · Issue #24781 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"35b34a6fe482eefb\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24806/linked_closing_reference?reference_location=REPO_ISSUES_INDEX","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ef59f929393b81b3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Discord Plugin unavailable during fresh install · Issue #24781 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Discord Plugin unavailable during fresh install #24781. [[Bug]: Discord Plugin unavailable during fresh install](#top)#24781. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. ## Description. opened on Feb 23, 2026. ### Summary. During a fresh VPS install, selecting Discord (BOT API) under channel selection fails to install. ### Steps to reproduce. 1. Fresh Debian 13 install on VPS. 2. Run curl -fsSL  | sh. 3. Setup via guided onboarding. 4. Get to Channel Selection step. 6. Input Discord Bot API key. 7. See Channel Setup: \"discord plugin not available.\". ### Expected behavior. 1. Input discord API key. 2. Continue with discord setup. ### Actual behavior. ### OpenClaw version. ### Operating system. ### Install method. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. ### Additional information. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't working. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ef59f929393b81b3\">>>","score":0.99991655},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bfc0143b6a6165ca\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Discord plugin fails with \"fetch failed\" when using proxy · Issue #42702 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bfc0143b6a6165ca\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/42702","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8b1b4cebf02a8b99\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nYou signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. # [Bug]: Discord plugin fails with \"fetch failed\" when using proxy #42702. [[Bug]: Discord plugin fails with \"fetch failed\" when using proxy](#top)#42702. Discord plugin shows `ON | OK` but health check shows `fetch failed`. Proxy setting (`channels.discord.proxy`) not applied to REST API calls. 1. Configure `channels.discord.proxy` in OpenClaw config. 3. Verify proxy works: `curl -x $PROXY https://discord.com/api/...` ✅. 4. Run `openclaw message send --channel=discord ...`. ### Expected behavior. When `channels.discord.proxy` is configured, all Discord HTTP requests (REST. API + WebSocket) should route through the proxy. * `channels.discord.proxy` is only applied to WebSocket connections, not. + `openclaw status` shows `ON | OK` for Discord plugin, but health check. + `openclaw message send --channel=discord` times out or fails with `fetch failed` in proxy-required environments. `openclaw-tui` (CLI) → OpenClaw Gateway → `discord` channel (via `channels.discord.proxy`). ### Additional provider/model setup details. No fields configured for issues without a type.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8b1b4cebf02a8b99\">>>","score":0.99990237}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775088284148}}
